.TH AGENTBAR 1 "" "agentbar" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agentbar \- connect Claude Code to the AgentBar GNOME top-bar indicator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agentbar install-hooks
.RB [ \-\-apply ]
.RB [ \-\-settings
.IR path ]
.br
.B agentbar uninstall-hooks
.RB [ \-\-apply ]
.RB [ \-\-settings
.IR path ]
.br
.B agentbar doctor
.RB [ \-\-settings
.IR path ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
AgentBar shows what each Claude Code session is doing in the GNOME Shell top
bar. Claude Code reports its activity through hooks; this command adds, removes,
and checks those hooks. Nothing leaves the machine.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install-hooks
Print the hook configuration AgentBar would add to Claude Code's settings and
change nothing. With
.BR \-\-apply ,
back up the settings file next to itself, then add one AgentBar handler per
Claude Code hook event, keeping every other setting and hook.
.TP
.B uninstall-hooks
Preview, or with
.B \-\-apply
remove, only the handlers AgentBar added.
.TP
.B doctor
Check the installation read-only and print one PASS, WARN, or FAIL line per
check. Exits 1 if a required check fails. The output names no session,
project, or settings content.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.claude/settings.json
Claude Code settings, or
.I $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/settings.json
when that variable is set.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/agentbar/
AgentBar state: the current snapshot and the event history.
.SH NOTES
After installing hooks, restart Claude Code. A newly installed GNOME extension
is found at the next login; enable it with
.BR "gnome-extensions enable agentbar@ameghcoder.github.io" .
Removing the package leaves the hooks and state in place; run
.B agentbar uninstall-hooks \-\-apply
first.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR agentbar-hook (1)
